-- 9.3 Compositional ordering & earliest content (docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub §4 alone vs given §§1-2)
sample-sec4 : List Word
sample-sec4 = "**4. Meaning is transport.** Each selected occurrence e came with what followed it, r(e): what i did next, what happened next, what was said next. A path p : c(e) = c_t transports it to the present. The meaning of the present occurrence is the family M_i(w, t) = Σ_{(e,p) : Sel_i(w,t)} transport_p(r(e)). The meaning is determinate when the transported family is contractible, every selected continuation agreeing up to a path. An ambiguity is a family that is not contractible: one occurrence whose possible contexts transport different continuations. Context resolves an ambiguity by shrinking the fiber, never by weighting it."
